<.shell current={:combobox}>
  <h1>Combobox</h1>
  <p class="lead">A select you type into, for a long list.</p>

  <div class="demo">
    <form class="measure" onsubmit="return false">
      <.input
        type="combobox"
        id="combobox-demo"
        name="qualification-id"
        label="Add a qualification"
        value=""
        options={qualification_options()}
      />
      <.button type="button">Add qualification</.button>
    </form>
  </div>

  <h3>Small, with groups</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <form class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2" onsubmit="return false">
      <select class="input-sm" aria-label="In or Not in">
        <option>In</option>
        <option>Not in</option>
      </select>
      <.combobox
        id="combobox-demo-sm"
        name="target"
        size={:sm}
        options={rule_options()}
        aria-label="Group or endorsement"
      />
      <.button type="button" size={:sm}>Add rule</.button>
    </form>
  </div>

  <h3 id="free-text">Free text</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <form class="max-w-xs" onsubmit="return false">
      <.input
        type="combobox"
        id="combobox-demo-free"
        name="role"
        label="Role (optional)"
        value="GSTL"
        options={["MIT", "GSTL", "Member", "Search Manager"]}
        free_text
      />
    </form>
  </div>

  <h3 id="hints">Short list, with hints</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <form class="measure" onsubmit="return false">
      <.input
        type="combobox"
        id="combobox-demo-hints"
        name="category"
        label="Category"
        value="maintenance"
        placeholder="Select a category"
        keyboard={false}
        options={[
          [
            key: "Administrative Work",
            value: "admin",
            "data-hint": "Phone calls, emails, and filing"
          ],
          [
            key: "Maintenance",
            value: "maintenance",
            "data-hint": "Vehicles, equipment, and the hall"
          ],
          [
            key: "Training Prep",
            value: "training",
            "data-hint": "eLearning and solo rope practice"
          ]
        ]}
      >
        <:below>
          <p class="hint mt-1">Vehicles, equipment, and the hall</p>
        </:below>
      </.input>
    </form>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    A list that can run past about 15 options, such as a team's qualifications, groups, or endorsements.
  </p>
  <p>
    With <code>free_text</code>, an answer people usually pick from what the team already uses but may type new, such as a member's role. The options are the team's own answers, most used first.
  </p>

  <p>
    With hints and <code>keyboard=&#123;false&#125;</code>, a short list whose choices need a line each to explain, where radios would fill a phone's screen, such as a chore's category. Show the picked one's hint under the box.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A short, fixed list, such as a year, a status, or a sort. Use a select.</li>
    <li>
      A list too big to send with the page, such as equipment or members. Search on the server and show the matches in a
      <a href={page_path(:table)}>table</a>
      with an Add button on each row.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Typing lists the options with every word typed, in any order, and underlines them.</li>
    <li>Clicking the box, or the down arrow, lists every option.</li>
    <li>The arrow keys move through the list. Enter picks one, and Escape closes the list.</li>
    <li>
      Text left without a pick is cleared, so the form never sends a guess. With free text it stays, and is what the form sends; nothing is highlighted until the arrow keys move, so Enter keeps it.
    </li>
    <li>The x at the end clears the box and lists every option again.</li>
    <li>Groups of options show under a heading each.</li>
    <li>An option's hint shows as a muted line under its label.</li>
    <li>
      With <code>keyboard=&#123;false&#125;</code>, tapping the box on a phone opens the list, not the keyboard.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.input type="combobox" options=&#123;…&#125; label="…" /&gt;</code>
    takes the same options as a select, and the form gets the same params. A hidden select holds the value, so a test fills it in as a select.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>free_text</code>
    makes the text box the field instead, and the hidden select only holds the suggestions. Change member uses it for Role.
  </p>
  <p>
    An option written as <code>[key: "Maintenance", value: id, "data-hint": "…"]</code>
    carries its hint. Log a chore uses it for Category.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.combobox size=&#123;:sm&#125; aria-label="…" /&gt;</code>
    in a row of small controls with no label.
  </p>
</.shell>
